The package includes data and code from third parties:

1. IOC World Bird List v15.2
   Files: inst/extdata/taxonomy/ioc_15.2_birds.csv.gz and the IOC names of
   inst/extdata/taxonomy/birdnet_v2.4_to_ioc_15.2.csv.gz.
   Gill F, D Donsker & P Rasmussen (Eds). 2026. IOC World Bird List (v15.2).
   https://www.worldbirdnames.org
   Licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported License
   (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/).

2. BirdNET v2.4 labels
   The scientific and English names of inst/extdata/taxonomy/
   birdnet_v2.4_to_ioc_15.2.csv.gz come from the labels of the BirdNET v2.4
   model (https://zenodo.org/records/15050749), by the K. Lisa Yang Center
   for Conservation Bioacoustics (Cornell Lab of Ornithology) and Chemnitz
   University of Technology, licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The models
   themselves are not distributed with AudiomothR: birdnetR downloads them.

3. Values accepted by Observation.org
   File: inst/extdata/observation_values.csv. Values of the columns method,
   counting method and activity of the Observation.org import example
   (observations-import-example.xlsx, https://observation.org), in Spanish.

4. Names of the bird species of Observation.org
   File: inst/extdata/taxonomy/observation_birds.csv.gz and the column
   obs_name of birdnet_v2.4_to_ioc_15.2.csv.gz. Scientific names taken from
   the species list of Observation.org (https://observation.org), downloaded
   on 2026-10-28, used to export records that its import accepts.

5. Biosonora
   The reading of CONFIG.TXT and of the metadata of WAV files (R/config.R,
   R/wav.R) was adapted from code of the Biosonora project, by Antonio
   Canepa-Oneto (author and maintainer of AudiomothR).
